{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"sd-card","name":"SD card module","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"A micro-SD card module (SPI) for keeping data: log readings to a file, read them back. The card holds its files while the run lasts (stop the run and it's a fresh card; its files are listed in the run panel). Includes SD.h.","category":"Storage","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// SD card module. A real card speaks the SD protocol over SPI; this one speaks a short request /\n// answer protocol of its own (the included SD.h knows it): a request [0xB5, op, length (2 bytes),\n// bytes...], then [0xB6, 0xFF...] to clock its answer out ([length (2 bytes), bytes...]).\n// ops: 1 card? 2 exists 3 remove 4 size 5 read(at, n) 6 append 7 truncate 8 list 9 mkdir\nconst MAX_FILE = 256 * 1024, MAX_FILES = 64;\n\nbench.device('sd', (part) => {\n  const card = part.params.card !== false;\n  const files = new Map(); // name -> bytes\n  let powered = false, answer = [], ops = 0;\n  const text = (b) => String.fromCharCode(...b);\n  const u32 = (n) => [n & 255, (n >> 8) & 255, (n >> 16) & 255, (n >>> 24) & 255];\n  const rd32 = (b, i) => (b[i] | (b[i + 1] << 8) | (b[i + 2] << 16) | (b[i + 3] << 24)) >>> 0;\n  const norm = (n) => n.replace(/^\\/+/, '').toLowerCase();\n  const total = () => [...files.values()].reduce((s, f) => s + f.length, 0);\n  const handle = (op, b) => {\n    ops++;\n    if (!card) return [0];\n    if (op === 1) return [1];\n    // the name comes first: its length, then its characters\n    const nl = b[0] ?? 0, name = norm(text(b.slice(1, 1 + nl))), rest = b.slice(1 + nl);\n    if (op === 2) return [files.has(name) || [...files.keys()].some((k) => k.startsWith(name + '/')) || name === '' ? 1 : 0];\n    if (op === 3) return [files.delete(name) ? 1 : 0];\n    if (op === 4) return files.has(name) ? [1, ...u32(files.get(name).length)] : [0];\n    if (op === 5) {\n      const f = files.get(name);\n      if (!f) return [0];\n      const at = rd32(rest, 0), n = Math.min(rd32(rest, 4), 400);\n      return [1, ...f.slice(at, at + n)];\n    }\n    if (op === 6) {\n      let f = files.get(name);\n      if (!f) { if (files.size >= MAX_FILES) return [0]; f = []; files.set(name, f); }\n      if (f.length + rest.length > MAX_FILE) return [0];\n      f.push(...rest);\n      return [1];\n    }\n    if (op === 7) { files.set(name, []); return [1]; }\n    if (op === 8) {\n      const names = [...files.keys()].filter((k) => k.startsWith(name ? name + '/' : '')).map((k) => k.slice(name ? name.length + 1 : 0)).join('\\n');\n      return [1, ...Array.from(names.slice(0, 390), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0))];\n    }\n    if (op === 9) return [1];\n    return [0];\n  };\n  return {\n    spi: {\n      transfer(bytes) {\n        if (!powered) return bytes.map(() => 0xff);\n        if (bytes[0] === 0xb5) {\n          const len = (bytes[2] ?? 0) | ((bytes[3] ?? 0) << 8);\n          const r = handle(bytes[1], bytes.slice(4, 4 + len));\n          answer = [r.length & 255, r.length >> 8, ...r];\n          return bytes.map(() => 0xff);\n        }\n        if (bytes[0] === 0xb6) {\n          const out = [0xff, ...answer.slice(0, bytes.length - 1)];\n          while (out.length < bytes.length) out.push(0xff);\n          return out;\n        }\n        return bytes.map(() => 0xff);\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 3.2;\n      io.draw(powered ? (ops ? 0.03 : 0.005) : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      if (!card) return ['no card in it'];\n      const list = [...files].map(([n, f]) => `${n} (${f.length} bytes)`);\n      return [list.length ? `${files.size} file(s), ${total()} bytes` : 'empty card', ...list.slice(0, 6)];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"SD.h":{"classes":["File"],"exports":["SD","FILE_READ","FILE_WRITE","O_READ","O_WRITE","O_APPEND","O_CREAT"],"code":"// SD.h: SD.begin(CS);  File f = SD.open(\"log.txt\", FILE_WRITE);  f.println(x);  f.close();\r\n//   File f = SD.open(\"log.txt\");  while (f.available()) Serial.write(f.read());  f.close();\r\n//   SD.exists(name), SD.remove(name), SD.mkdir(name);  f.size(), f.position(), f.seek(n), f.peek(),\r\n//   f.readStringUntil('\\n'), f.name();  File root = SD.open(\"/\"); root.openNextFile()\r\n// FILE_WRITE adds to the end of the file (as Arduino's does). It talks to the module over SPI.\r\nconst FILE_READ = 1, FILE_WRITE = 0x13, O_READ = 1, O_WRITE = 2, O_APPEND = 4, O_CREAT = 0x10;\r\n\r\nconst _sd = { cs: -1, ok: false };\r\nconst _sdCall = (op, name = '', data = []) => {\r\n  const nb = Array.from(String(name).slice(0, 60), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0) & 255);\r\n  const body = [nb.length, ...nb, ...data];\r\n  digitalWrite(_sd.cs, LOW);\r\n  SPI.transfer([0xb5, op, body.length & 255, body.length >> 8, ...body]);\r\n  digitalWrite(_sd.cs, HIGH);\r\n  digitalWrite(_sd.cs, LOW);\r\n  const r = SPI.transfer([0xb6, ...new Array(410).fill(0xff)]);\r\n  digitalWrite(_sd.cs, HIGH);\r\n  const len = r[1] | (r[2] << 8);\r\n  if (r[1] === 0xff && r[2] === 0xff) return null; // (nothing answered: no card module on the bus)\r\n  return r.slice(3, 3 + len);\r\n};\r\nconst _u32 = (n) => [n & 255, (n >> 8) & 255, (n >> 16) & 255, (n >>> 24) & 255];\r\n\r\nclass File {\r\n  constructor(name = '', write = false, dir = false) {\r\n    this._name = name; this._write = write; this._dir = dir; this._pos = 0; this._open = !!name || dir; this._buf = []; this._list = null;\r\n    this._cache = []; this._cacheAt = -1; this._size = -1;\r\n  }\r\n  /** the byte at the read position, from a 256-byte window read ahead (one SPI exchange per window) */\r\n  _byte(at) {\r\n    if (this._cacheAt < 0 || at < this._cacheAt || at >= this._cacheAt + this._cache.length) {\r\n      const r = _sdCall(5, this._name, [..._u32(at), ..._u32(256)]);\r\n      this._cache = r && r[0] ? r.slice(1) : [];\r\n      this._cacheAt = at;\r\n    }\r\n    const i = at - this._cacheAt;\r\n    return i < this._cache.length ? this._cache[i] : -1;\r\n  }\r\n  name() { return this._name.split('/').pop(); }\r\n  isDirectory() { return this._dir; }\r\n  size() {\r\n    this.flush();\r\n    if (this._size < 0) { const r = _sdCall(4, this._name); this._size = r && r[0] ? (r[1] | (r[2] << 8) | (r[3] << 16) | (r[4] << 24)) >>> 0 : 0; }\r\n    return this._size;\r\n  }\r\n  position() { return this._pos; }\r\n  seek(n) { this._pos = Math.max(0, n); return true; }\r\n  available() { return this._open && !this._write ? Math.max(0, this.size() - this._pos) : 0; }\r\n  read(buf, n) {\r\n    if (buf !== undefined && typeof buf === 'object') {\r\n      let k = 0;\r\n      for (; k < n; k++) { const b = this._byte(this._pos); if (b < 0) break; buf[k] = b; this._pos++; }\r\n      return k;\r\n    }\r\n    const b = this._byte(this._pos);\r\n    if (b >= 0) this._pos++;\r\n    return b;\r\n  }\r\n  peek() { return this._byte(this._pos); }\r\n  readStringUntil(end) {\r\n    let s = '';\r\n    for (;;) {\r\n      const b = this._byte(this._pos);\r\n      if (b < 0) return s;\r\n      this._pos++;\r\n      const ch = String.fromCharCode(b);\r\n      if (ch === end) return s;\r\n      s += ch;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  readString() { return this.readStringUntil('\\u0000'); }\r\n  write(x, n) {\r\n    if (!this._write) return 0;\r\n    const bytes = typeof x === 'string' ? Array.from(x, (c) => c.charCodeAt(0) & 255) : x && typeof x === 'object' ? Array.from(x).slice(0, n ?? x.length).map((b) => Number(b) & 255) : [Number(x) & 255];\r\n    this._buf.push(...bytes);\r\n    if (this._buf.length >= 256) this.flush();\r\n    return bytes.length;\r\n  }\r\n  print(x = '', f) {\r\n    let s;\r\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && f !== undefined) s = f === 16 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(16).toUpperCase() : f === 2 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(2) : f === 10 ? String(Math.trunc(x)) : x.toFixed(f);\r\n    else if (typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x)) s = x.toFixed(2);\r\n    else s = String(x);\r\n    return this.write(s);\r\n  }\r\n  println(x = '', f) { return this.print(x, f) + this.write('\\r\\n'); }\r\n  flush() {\r\n    while (this._buf.length) {\r\n      const chunk = this._buf.splice(0, 300);\r\n      _sdCall(6, this._name, chunk);\r\n      this._pos += chunk.length;\r\n      this._size = -1;\r\n      this._cacheAt = -1;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  close() { this.flush(); this._open = false; }\r\n  openNextFile() {\r\n    if (!this._dir) return null;\r\n    if (!this._list) { const r = _sdCall(8, this._name); this._list = r && r[0] ? String.fromCharCode(...r.slice(1)).split('\\n').filter(Boolean) : []; }\r\n    const n = this._list.shift();\r\n    return n ? new File((this._name ? this._name + '/' : '') + n, false) : null;\r\n  }\r\n  rewindDirectory() { this._list = null; }\r\n  valueOf() { return this._open; }\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst SD = {\r\n  begin(cs = SS) {\r\n    _sd.cs = cs;\r\n    pinMode(cs, OUTPUT);\r\n    digitalWrite(cs, HIGH);\r\n    SPI.begin();\r\n    const r = _sdCall(1);\r\n    _sd.ok = !!r && r[0] === 1;\r\n    return _sd.ok;\r\n  },\r\n  exists(name) { const r = _sdCall(2, name); return !!r && r[0] === 1; },\r\n  remove(name) { const r = _sdCall(3, name); return !!r && r[0] === 1; },\r\n  mkdir(name) { const r = _sdCall(9, name); return !!r && r[0] === 1; },\r\n  rmdir(name) { return this.remove(name); },\r\n  /** a File, or null if it can't (no card, or reading one that isn't there): check it with if (f) */\r\n  open(name, mode = FILE_READ) {\r\n    if (!_sd.ok) return null;\r\n    const n = String(name).replace(/^\\/+/, '');\r\n    if (n === '') return new File('', false, true);\r\n    const write = (mode & O_WRITE) !== 0;\r\n    if (!write && !this.exists(n)) return null;\r\n    const f = new File(n, write);\r\n    if (write) {\r\n      if (!(mode & O_APPEND) && (mode & O_CREAT) && mode !== FILE_WRITE) _sdCall(7, n);\r\n      _sdCall(6, n, []);\r\n      f._pos = f.size();\r\n    }\r\n    return f;\r\n  },\r\n};\r\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"sd","name":"SD card module","description":"SPI: CS to any pin (SD.begin(CS)), SCK, MOSI, MISO to the board's SPI pins; VCC (5 V, it has its own 3.3 V regulator) and GND. #include <SD.h>; File f = SD.open(\"log.txt\", FILE_WRITE); f.println(value); f.close();","swatch":"#1d4fb8","mass":4,"params":[{"key":"card","label":"Card in it","kind":"bool"}],"defaults":{"card":true},"shape":[{"box":[2.4,0.16,4.2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[1.5,0.2,1.6],"at":[0,0.26,1.2],"color":"#c9cdd4"},{"box":[1.1,0.06,1.5],"at":[0,0.39,1.3],"color":"#1a1a1c","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","VCC","MISO","MOSI","SCK","CS"],"at":[-0.635,0,-1.85],"kinds":{"GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin","MISO":"out","MOSI":"in","SCK":"in","CS":"in"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (4.5-5.5 V)","vmin":3.2,"vmax":5.5}}}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"MOSI","miso":"MISO","cs":"CS"},"device":"sd"}],"examples":[{"name":"Data logger","description":"Logs the knob's reading to log.csv twice a second; every 10 lines it reads the whole file back and prints it. Press Run and turn the knob.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Data logger","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"sd","type":"sd-card/sd","name":"SD card","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[5,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Knob","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP17"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"CS"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP18"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"SCK"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP19"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"MOSI"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP16"},"b":{"uid":"sd","pin":"MISO"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Data logger: the knob's reading goes into log.csv on the SD card twice a second; every 10 lines\n// the whole file is read back and printed. Turn the knob (its slider in the run panel).\n#include <SPI.h>\n#include <SD.h>\n\n#define SD_CS 17\nint lines = 0;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!SD.begin(SD_CS)) {\n    Serial.println(\"No SD card: check the module's wires (and that a card is in it)\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n  if (SD.exists(\"log.csv\")) SD.remove(\"log.csv\");\n  File f = SD.open(\"log.csv\", FILE_WRITE);\n  f.println(\"time_ms,knob\");\n  f.close();\n  Serial.println(\"logging to log.csv\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  File f = SD.open(\"log.csv\", FILE_WRITE);\n  if (f) {\n    f.print(millis());\n    f.print(\",\");\n    f.println(analogRead(A0));\n    f.close();\n    lines++;\n  }\n  if (lines % 10 == 0) {\n    Serial.println(\"--- log.csv so far ---\");\n    File r = SD.open(\"log.csv\");\n    while (r.available()) Serial.write(r.read());\n    r.close();\n  }\n  delay(500);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}